message: "If you use this in your research or tooling, please cite it as below."
title: "mri-research: A curated knowledge hub for magnetic resonance imaging research"
abstract: >-
  A curated, verified reference hub that gives an AI coding agent fluent
  orientation across the whole magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) research
  pipeline: MR physics and k-space foundations; acquisition, pulse-sequence and
  trajectory design; image reconstruction (parallel imaging, compressed
  sensing, low-rank, deep learning, diffusion/score-based, MR fingerprinting)
  and reconstruction toolboxes; raw and image data formats and open datasets;
  image analysis and processing (structural, functional, and diffusion MRI,
  segmentation, registration); quantitative MRI and spectroscopy; MRI hardware;
  and programmatic literature access. It points to the community's primary
  resources rather than bundling datasets or copyrighted text. Built for AI
  agents, its aim is to make the MRI community's collective knowledge accessible
  to everyone. It ships as a team of specialized agent skills — reconstruction
  (actionable via BART/SigPy), diffusion MRI, pulse-sequence design,
  deep-learning reconstruction, and hardware — alongside a generalist hub and an
  end-to-end research-workflow assistant that takes a study from idea to a
  published paper (CVPR, MICCAI, MRM).
